to 1, PHP will send 
RFC 2616 compliant headers. 

If this option is enabled, 
and you are running PHP in 
a CGI environment 
(e.g. PHP-FPM) you should 
not use standard RFC 2616 
style HTTP status response 
headers, you should 
instead use their RFC 3875 
equivalent e.g. instead of 
header("HTTP/1.0 404 Not found"); 
you should use 
header("Status: 404 Not Found");

